    "done_when": "Each of these callers stops parsing timestamps itself and calls reckon._timestamps.parse_utc: reckon/_backends.py:_parse_cached_fetch_stamp, reckon/_backends.py:_event_timestamp, reckon/budget.py:_parse_stamp, reckon/crew/budget_group.py:_observed_moment, reckon/crew/metering.py:_event_timestamp, reckon/crew/metering.py:_stamped_elapsed, reckon/crew/ticker.py:row_moment, reckon/crew/ticker.py:local_clock. ticker.local_clock renders the reader's wall clock for display and keeps that behaviour exactly.\n\nBefore editing, record each caller's current output at base cea6da07 by running the base code, never by writing what you expect. Use one shared input list:\n- an aware ISO string, a Z-suffixed string and a lowercase-z string;\n- a space-separated zoned stamp (2026-09-29 01:02:03+00:00) and a space-separated naive stamp;\n- an offset carrying seconds (2026-09-29T01:02:03+00:00:30);\n- a near-midnight offset (2024-03-05T00:30:00+02:00);\n- a naive string, a date-only string, and a valid date followed by trailing text (2024-03-05bogus);\n- a string with surrounding whitespace;\n- an epoch number, an empty string, None, a non-string object and garbage text.\nRecord a raised exception's type as that input's output.\n\nA caller whose semantics differ from parse_utc keeps its base output for every input, either with a line or two around the call, or as a retained exception with its reason. Such a caller consumes a stated calendar date, validates a strict spelling, or renders for display. A private helper left with no caller is deleted, and the fragment names it.\n\nA second test walks the touched modules with ast and asserts that no fromisoformat call remains outside the retained exceptions the table names.\n\nThat file, tests/test_timestamps_parse_utc.py, and the existing test file of each touched module that has one pass at exit 0. The manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. Each arm runs at its named revision, and the head arm at the committed head. Every gate log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command. Any failing id in an arm is listed in failure_attribution as present at base or as caused. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. The full project suite is not run by this node.\nThe expectations are committed as tests/test_timestamp_callers_batch_c.py.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
